			<div class="content" id="post-content-4824867">
									

<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Comedy/Horror(?)</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP researchers discover that after staring at the chest area of one of their female co-workers for over ten seconds, the word &quot;M I N E&quot; seems to appear on it etched in blood, changing the observer's eye color to an alarming shade of magenta and causing blindness if they continue staring.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> People frequently wondered why Dr. Jenna Lopez never seemed to mind that Dr. Briggs kept staring at her chest. Strangely, if anyone mentioned his ogling, both doctors would deny that he was ever looking, both appearing confused by the suggestion that such an event had ever occurred, until the events of August 9th, 2020. That day, at lunch in the cafeteria, Dr. Briggs was &quot;enjoying the view&quot;, when suddenly, he started screaming. Co-workers turned to him, only to find that his irises had turned a viciously-bright shade of magenta. He, in a panicked frenzy, claimed that this was the first time he had ever looked at her chest, then vehemently insisted that he'd seen the word &quot;M I N E&quot; appear on her as if carved into the exposed skin. Other researchers, including Dr. Lopez herself, glanced down, only to see nothing of the sort. Briggs tried to insist again, continuing to look at her as the security team was called, only for him to start screaming again, this time out of intense pain rather than shock. Briggs then went fully blind. Lopez was temporarily confined, and tests started being performed.</p>
<p>Note: Lopez seems to completely lack control or intention regarding these effects, such that SCP-XXXX is identified as solely her chest, rather than the woman herself.</p>
<p><strong>Containment:</strong> Since only exposed skin seems to cause the effects described, Lopez is allowed to roam free so long as she continues to wear clothing that covers her bosom (as well as an SCP-commissioned undergarment to prevent the effects from seeping through non-opaque fabrics). The classification is, for the time being, safe.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> First, the humor and righteousness of an SCP that punishes perverts who stare at this poor woman's chest. Second, the idea and potential ethical debate of an SCP attached to a non-SCP human person.</p>

